{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user provided a detailed automated \"stitch\" task (Task ID: 5120) to implement the `pkg/testutils` package for the go-unix-utils project. This package provides the differential testing harness that all cmd/ utilities use to compare their output against GNU reference binaries. The task requires creating two files: `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (DiffTest struct, NormalizeFunc, RunDiffTests, ComposeNormalizers, TimestampNormalizer) and `pkg/testutils/build.go` (BuildBinary helper). The implementation must follow exact contract signatures from srd001-testutils, set LC_ALL=C for locale-independent comparison, use t.Run for subtests, and not import any cmd/ or other pkg/ packages.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: run Go binary and GNU reference binary side-by-side, compare stdout/stderr/exit code\n   - NormalizeFunc is a type ALIAS (`type NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte`), not a type definition\n   - BuildBinary compiles cmd/ packages using `go build` within the Go module, using t.TempDir() for automatic cleanup\n   - LC_ALL=C must be set in environment for both binaries (Design Decision D1)\n   - RunDiffTests uses t.Run for named subtests (Design Decision D4)\n   - Package must not import any cmd/ or other pkg/ packages (Design Decision D3)\n   - TimestampNormalizer replaces common timestamp patterns (ISO 8601, month-day-time, HH:MM:SS) with `<TIMESTAMP>` placeholder\n   - Go module path: `github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils`\n   - 40-line function size limit enforced by execution constitution article E8\n   - Git is managed externally - no git commands allowed\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `pkg/testutils/build.go` (SUCCESSFULLY CREATED)\n     - Contains